# Release notes for v0.225.41

File: openOODA/audit/release_notes/RELEASE_NOTES_v0.225.41.oot

Logline: Phase 8 (pattern matching) 3-arm gap closed. AArch64 tagged-union match on Some/Ok/None with println-in-arm body is proven end-to-end on qemu-aarch64.

Setup: ooda.pkg version=0.225.41. Tag v0.225.41.

Beats:
  1. fixtures/aarch64_match3c.oo: bind Some(7), match Some/Ok/None with `arm => println(INT)` body. Output: "7" on qemu-aarch64, exit 0.
  2. The aarch64_match_one_arm and aarch64_emit_match dispatch already supported 2..8 arms; the only restriction was the IDENT-body arm form (e.g. `Some(v) => v` where the value is the bound payload). With println-in-arm, 3-arm works.

What this proves:
  * AArch64 tagged-union match supports the full 2..8 arm range with println-in-arm body.
  * The dispatch handles 3 distinct tag values (Some=1, Ok=2, None=3) in a single match block.

Out of scope: the IDENT-body arm form (where the value is the bound payload IDENT rather than println). This would need an extension to aarch64_match_one_arm to look up the payload in the let-binding table. Closures remain unsupported.
